    "title": "Sabres close to trading JJ Peterka to Western Conference foe in surprise NHL trade - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Buffalo wing JJ Peterka has been involved in trade rumors for a while now. It looks like they might be coming to fruition for the talented Sabres forward. Daily Faceoff's Frank Seravalli has reported that Peterka will be sent to the Utah Mammoth in a trade, if an unreported contingency is met. MORE: Gavin McKenna choosing between four college hockey teams Peterka is still just 23 years old. The young German right wing was a second-round pick in 2020. He's coming off a career year. He had 27 goals and 41 assists for 68 points in 77 games. The Sabres seem stuck in an eternal rebuild, so why not trade an on-the-rise 23-year old? The Mammoth, with their new name, are trying to build up their organization, and Peterka would be a great foundational piece as some secondary scoring. It's not clear what still needs to happen to make this deal go through, but it'd be a big deal if it does. MORE NHL NEWS:",
